                {
                    "kind": "source",
                    "item": {
                        "id": "winnifred-eaton-reeve/his-royal-nibs",
                        "source_id": "standardebooks",
                        "series_identity": "winnifred-eaton-reeve/his-royal-nibs",
                        "title": "His Royal Nibs",
                        "cover_url": "/sources/standardebooks/series/winnifred-eaton-reeve%2Fhis-royal-nibs/cover",
                        "chapter_count": 28,
                        "genres": [
                            "Fiction"
                        ],
                        "status": "completed",
                        "description": "A young man dubbed \u201cCheerio\u201d for his English background, clean appearance, and well-kept suit, unexpectedly arrives at the highly regarded O Bar O ranch with one goal in mind: to offer his services as a hired hand, and thus find a new start in life in a foreign land. The ranch\u2019s foreman, Bully Bill, surprised and irritated by the unwelcome stranger, decides to give Cheerio the job after witnessing his cool composure in the presence of a startled herd, preventing the ranch owner\u2019s son from getting injured.\n\nCheerio proves his worth at every opportunity and earns the respect, both honest and begrudging, from riders and cowpunchers alike. His hard working day-to-day routine is balanced by his developing friendship with the boy he saved, Sandy McPherson, and the boy\u2019s sister Hilda, for whom Cheerio develops a liking and who has become the subject of Cheerio\u2019s artistic endeavors.\n\nEverything seems to be going well for Cheerio until an incident at the branding corral brings back uncomfortable memories of his past life. Being deemed a coward and a weak man by his boss and peers, Cheerio grasps at one final chance to redeem himself and achieve his dream: to play a nightly game of chess with Canadian champion and famous rancher P. D. McPherson.\n\nHis Royal Nibs is a story of resilience, newfound love, and fresh beginnings inspired by Winnifred Eaton Reeve\u2019s desire to write fiction set in Alberta, Canada after a career spent writing Japanese-themed works under a variety of pseudonyms, the most famous of which being \u201cOnoto Watanna.\u201d His Royal Nibs would turn out to be her last published novel.",
